-----------------

Yes — and this is exactly the right time to name the pieces before the architecture hardens.

I would separate these into **three lanes**:

```text
1. Personal brand
2. Product / platform brand
3. Mythic / seed / vessel brand
```

Because mixing those too early can make the story muddy.

## Your proposed domains

| Domain                 | My take                                                            | Strength                                             | Concern                                                                    |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `coresdeck.com`        | Useful, but slightly awkward                                       | Short-ish, available-sounding, close to Command Deck | “Coresdeck” is not instantly understandable; people may hear “course deck” |
| `auroracorebridge.com` | Strong concept, long domain                                        | Captures ACT Bridge idea clearly                     | Long, many syllables, easy to mistype                                      |
| `aurora-seed.com`      | Very good mythic/investment name                                   | Memorable, vessel/seed-investment resonance          | Hyphen is less ideal, but acceptable                                       |
| `paul-gutierrez.com`   | Good personal/project identity if Paul is the name you want public | Human, credible, portfolio-ready                     | Hyphen adds friction; also consider `.dev`, `.ai`, `.io`, `.net` variants  |

One practical warning: domain registration only gives you the right to use the name as a domain through a registrar; it does **not** automatically clear trademark risk. Domain names are registered through accredited registrars/registries, while trademark clearance is a separate legal/brand search process. ([Wikipedia][1]) For anything you may commercialize, do at least a basic United States Patent and Trademark Office search and web search before committing hard; a real trademark attorney is worth it before launch. ([Wikipedia][2])

## My recommendation

I would not lead with `coresdeck.com`.

I would lead with something closer to the actual platform promise:

```text
AuroraCore
AuroraBridge
AuroraCommand
AuroraDeck
CoreBridge
CommandBridge
```

The best product names need to answer quickly:

```text
What is it?
Who is it for?
What does it do?
Why does it feel different?
```

`coresdeck.com` feels internally meaningful but externally unclear. It may become useful as a module name, but I would not make it the flagship unless you love it.

