godaddy want to charge through the nose for any .ai domain for some reason... all the names you suggest are taken boss, thats why the ones I listed seem a bit wonky, they were "whats left"... I do like the idea of the .ai since these will ALL have ai built in in the near future

-----------------

Yep — that is the domain-name jungle now. The good `.ai` names are either taken, premium-priced, squatted, or priced like someone thinks every garage project is OpenAI by Tuesday.

The reason `.ai` hurts is partly structural: `.ai` is Anguilla’s country-code top-level domain, but it became the fashion domain for artificial-intelligence companies; available `.ai` domains have commonly carried much higher base/registrar fees than ordinary `.com`, and many registrars require or price around multi-year terms. ([Wikipedia][1]) GoDaddy also has a reputation for attractive first-year pricing plus higher renewals/upsells, so it is worth comparing registrars before buying. ([TechRadar][2]) Porkbun and Namecheap are often better places to compare “boring registrar” pricing and renewal costs, though availability and premium pricing will still bite. ([TechRadar][3])

Given that your first-choice names are taken, I’d use a **two-name strategy**:

```text
1. Cheap canonical .com/.org/.net for the durable project
2. One carefully chosen .ai only when it is worth the annual burn
```

Do not buy ten `.ai` domains unless money is loose. Buy one or two that are truly load-bearing.

