```

Like “pike” plus “sys.”

That gives it bite.

## Why it works better than random “cute” names

You were reacting against names like Google, Yahoo, GoDaddy, etc., where the name became valuable only after market saturation. Before the brand became famous, the word itself did little semantic work.

**Pykesys** is different. It is still somewhat quirky, but it has a root:

```text
Pike:
  spear, point, weapon/tool, old road, fish, mountain peak resonance

Sys:
  systems, sysadmin, syslog, syscall, Unix/Linux culture
```

So the name has a hidden engineer’s joke inside it. That is good.

It says:

```text
We are not a lifestyle app.
We are systems people.
```

