# Pykesys Business Plan: Three Layers

## Layer 1: Pykesys — The Business Core

**Purpose**

```text
Pykesys builds lawful systems for intelligent infrastructure.
```

Plain version:

```text
Pykesys designs, documents, prototypes, and supports command-oriented systems
for AI infrastructure, GPU operations, automation, and evidence-driven workflows.
```

### Core market

Initial customers are not “everyone.”

They are:

```text
small AI shops
GPU lab operators
startups running customer model pipelines
teams with expensive GPUs but weak operational discipline
companies building AI products without mature SRE practice
facilities that need command/control dashboards
```

These customers will have money because GPU work is expensive, but many will lack disciplined operations.

### Pain points

```text
GPU jobs fail halfway through pipelines.
Checkpoints exist but are poorly governed.
Schedulers are home-rolled.
Dashboards show product results but not operational truth.
Developers run devpods with unclear ownership.
GPU machines are expensive but treated like pets.
Customers pay for results, not excuses.
```

### Pykesys promise

```text
We help AI infrastructure teams turn fragile pipelines
into observable, recoverable, evidence-driven systems.
```

ACT version:

```text
Recognize the field.
Preserve lawful authority.
Act through a governed path.
Return evidence.
Feed memory.
Remain coherent under change.
```

### Initial services

| Service                              | Description                                                                    | Why It Sells                                      |
| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |
| AI Pipeline Reliability Review       | Review job lifecycle, checkpoints, artifacts, failure modes, dashboard handoff | Small AI shops need this immediately              |
| GPU Devpod / Workstation Standard    | Define reproducible GPU developer environments                                 | Prevents “works on my machine” chaos              |
| Checkpoint & Artifact Governance     | Map what gets saved, where, when, by whom, and how it resumes                  | Directly protects expensive compute cycles        |
| GPU Operations Glossary / Onboarding | Build training docs for teams entering GPU infrastructure                      | The engineer base is thin; onboarding is valuable |
| Command Dashboard Prototype          | Build a small operational dashboard showing jobs, stages, evidence, health     | First practical Command Deck seed                 |
| Runbook / Incident System            | Failure mode catalog, triage trees, recovery paths                             | SRE value, fast to deliver                        |
| Home-Lab-to-Prod Training            | Teach old cruisers how GPU/Kubernetes/AI pipelines work                        | You know this audience personally                 |

### First paid product shape

I would make the first Pykesys offering a packaged engagement:

